1
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:08,340
You're a murderer.

2
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:10,310
What?

3
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:15,250
Hey, Baek Mi Young, get back here.

4
00:00:25,490 --> 00:00:26,490
No.

5
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:29,630
You're worse than a murderer.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,970
(Complaint: Divorce, Alimony, Division Of Assets, Minor Children)

7
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:44,870
"Assault, profanity, verbal abuse, neglect, insults,"

8
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:46,740
"indifference toward the family,"

9
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:48,580
"irreconcilable personality differences,"

10
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:50,550
"and refusal of sexual relations?"

11
00:00:51,010 --> 00:00:52,680
Jeez, with all that, shouldn't you be going to jail,

12
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:53,880
not just getting a divorce?

13
00:00:55,850 --> 00:00:59,660
I knew Mi Young would pull something like this one day.

14
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:01,930
Putting on that innocent face in front of everyone,

15
00:01:02,090 --> 00:01:03,460
and then pulling this nonsense behind our backs?

16
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:06,830
What? Seven hundred ninety thousand as her share?

17
00:01:08,130 --> 00:01:10,200
Does she think 790,000 dollars is chump change?

18
00:01:10,730 --> 00:01:13,570
Come on, Mom. Let's hear Won Ho's side of the story first.

19
00:01:13,770 --> 00:01:15,840
Let's see if what Mi Young wrote in this is true or not.

20
00:01:16,170 --> 00:01:17,470
Of course it's not true.

21
00:01:17,670 --> 00:01:19,780
Do you really think any of what's written here makes sense?

22
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:23,280
- No, it doesn't make sense. - Won Ho, just trust me.

23
00:01:23,650 --> 00:01:26,420
I'll get you the best lawyer there is.

24
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:38,360
Don't make a mistake

25
00:01:38,430 --> 00:01:42,270
Find what you want to accomplish

26
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:46,100
Be brave and be strong

27
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:49,470
Let go of who you are today

28
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:52,980
Up into this beautiful blue sky

29
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:56,110
(Husband)

30
00:01:56,610 --> 00:01:58,920
- The number is unavailable... - Darn it.

31
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:03,720
This is why I was so against you two getting married.

32
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:05,320
Just think if you had listened to me back then.

33
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:06,920
Why would you be going through this awful mess?

34
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:09,530
You must be happy, Mom.

35
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:11,490
Since everything is going just the way you wanted.

36
00:02:11,630 --> 00:02:13,460
- What? - Didn't you see the complaint?

37
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:16,100
"Verbal abuse, neglect, insults, conflict with her mother-in-law."

38
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:19,170
Looks like all your hard work tormenting Mi Young paid off.

39
00:02:19,270 --> 00:02:20,300
What did you say, you brat?

40
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:22,470
This is all your fault, Mom. Because of you, now...

41
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:23,540
The nerve of this kid.

42
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:25,440
- Goodness. - Mom.

43
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:27,340
Right, this is going too far, isn't it?

44
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:29,510
Yes, Mom. That's going too far.

45
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:31,950
I should hit you with this. Come here, you jerk.

46
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,020
- My gosh. - Hey.

47
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:34,520
- Get over here. - You're going to kill me.

48
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:35,650
Don't you ever think of returning here.

49
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:36,720
You brat, I ought to...

50
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:42,430
- Two soup and rice, please. - Okay.

51
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:49,430
You're staying the night, right?

52
00:02:50,030 --> 00:02:51,030
Yes.

53
00:02:51,730 --> 00:02:52,740
And tomorrow?

54
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:54,700
Are you going back home tomorrow?

55
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:57,370
I'll stay at your motel for a while.

56
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:02,610
I'll pay for it.

57
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,650
Good grief...

58
00:03:10,850 --> 00:03:13,560
So, how did things get so bad between you and your wife?

59
00:03:14,790 --> 00:03:16,760
I don't know how things with Mi Young...

60
00:03:16,830 --> 00:03:17,990
got so twisted either.

61
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:21,760
I also have no clue what she was thinking...

62
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:23,530
when she sent that complaint.

63
00:03:23,930 --> 00:03:26,000
Come on, there must have been some warning signs before this.

64
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:29,340
Mi Young has always been the type to hold a grudge.

65
00:03:29,410 --> 00:03:32,010
She's the type to bottle up everything that upsets her.

66
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:35,110
And she's not the type to forgive easily,

67
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:36,310
no matter how hard I try.

68
00:03:36,980 --> 00:03:38,510
But you still should have tried.

69
00:03:38,650 --> 00:03:40,080
When you fight, you should just say you were wrong...

70
00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:41,320
and that you'll do much better from now on.

71
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:43,590
You should have just sucked it up and been the bigger person.

72
00:03:43,650 --> 00:03:45,020
It's so frustrating.

73
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:50,330
I'm telling you this because I couldn't do it myself.

74
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:54,000
But, Won Ho,

75
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:57,670
are the things in that complaint really true?

76
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:01,240
No. Absolutely not. How could I?

77
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:03,240
Right. Of course not, right?

78
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:04,770
Well, there's your answer.

79
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:06,680
Then there's no reason to give her an easy divorce.

80
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:19,820
The day I got divorced and came back home,

81
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:22,930
I found Mom in the bathroom washing a blanket.

82
00:04:23,890 --> 00:04:27,460
It was boiling hot, but she had a huge pile of winter blankets,

83
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:29,200
and she was beating them with a laundry stick.

84
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:33,300
Then suddenly, she started hitting her own chest with that stick.

85
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:36,610
She was crying, beating her chest with it.

86
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:39,910
Watching her do that...

87
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:42,380
My heart just...

88
00:04:46,780 --> 00:04:47,780
Mom.

89
00:04:48,820 --> 00:04:49,820
Mom...

90
00:04:51,290 --> 00:04:53,320
Hey, why are you crying?

91
00:04:53,620 --> 00:04:55,630
You jerk. You can't do that to Mom.

92
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:33,060
Are you happy?

93
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:36,270
Are you?

94
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:39,640
You...

95
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,170
Are you really doing okay?

96
00:06:01,990 --> 00:06:02,990
You...

97
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:05,560
You're worse than a murderer.

98
00:06:09,130 --> 00:06:11,600
Right, she's already cursing me out.

99
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,440
The complaint is nothing compared to that.

100
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:23,750
(Assault, Verbal Abuse, Profanity,)

101
00:06:23,810 --> 00:06:25,450
(Neglect, Insults, Conflict With In-Laws,)

102
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:26,780
(Indifference To The Family, Loss Of Affection,)

103
00:06:26,850 --> 00:06:28,020
(Lack Of Communication, Deep Divisions,)

104
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:29,120
(Refusal Of Sexual Relations)

105
00:06:30,250 --> 00:06:32,690
No, that's not right. Is that my fault?

106
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:34,460
Is that my fault?

107
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:03,590
He called me a kid.

108
00:07:03,890 --> 00:07:04,890
A kid?

109
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:07,790
CEO Ji.

110
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:09,190
He called me that.

111
00:07:09,790 --> 00:07:12,630
- "Wait." - That kid from Milan.

112
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:14,730
That's what he said.

113
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:18,430
Well, from his perspective, you probably do seem like a kid.

114
00:07:19,370 --> 00:07:20,840
It's a bit hard to see you as a woman...

115
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,710
Why? What's wrong with me?

116
00:07:23,870 --> 00:07:24,870
What's this?

117
00:07:25,510 --> 00:07:27,940
Don't tell me you like CEO Ji.

118
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:29,780
Well...

119
00:07:30,510 --> 00:07:32,250
It was intense when I first met him.

120
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:34,420
He's always surprising me,

121
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:36,290
and I wonder about him when he's not around.

122
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:40,190
Doesn't that mean I like him?

123
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:44,830
But still, he's CEO Baek's husband.

124
00:07:45,830 --> 00:07:46,830
Is he?

125
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:49,000
It looks like they're about to break up.

126
00:07:50,330 --> 00:07:51,330
What?

127
00:07:51,870 --> 00:07:55,440
I overheard him talking to a friend at a bar the other day.

128
00:07:55,870 --> 00:07:59,140
He said his wife asked for a divorce.

129
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:02,810
Then is that why Calvin did that?

130
00:08:03,780 --> 00:08:04,780
What do you mean?

131
00:08:04,850 --> 00:08:08,990
I gave CEO Baek the party invitation, remember?

132
00:08:09,790 --> 00:08:12,760
Calvin actually asked me to do that.

133
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:15,390
- Really? - He asked me...

134
00:08:15,390 --> 00:08:17,960
to make sure CEO Baek could come to the party.

135
00:08:19,030 --> 00:08:21,900
Isn't it because Calvin is interested in CEO Baek too?

136
00:08:23,130 --> 00:08:24,630
So that's what that was about.

137
00:08:25,130 --> 00:08:28,640
Anyway, even if you end up working with Calvin,

138
00:08:29,070 --> 00:08:30,710
you have to pretend you don't know anything about this.

139
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:32,810
Why would I work with him?

140
00:08:33,610 --> 00:08:36,050
Because you got a job there, that's why.

141
00:08:36,750 --> 00:08:38,250
I asked Calvin for a favour.

142
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:40,520
He said you should start tomorrow.

143
00:08:41,450 --> 00:08:43,450
You did? Oh, my gosh.

144
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:47,690
- Thank you so much. - You'll scare the baby.

145
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:50,030
Get away.

146
00:08:51,260 --> 00:08:55,430
As you know, Cheon Man Ju's wedding has been unavoidably postponed.

147
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:58,430
I know you were all looking forward to it...

148
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,540
and must be very disappointed,

149
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:00,970
but let's look forward to the next time.

150
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:03,510
Still, it's a good thing a life was saved.

151
00:09:04,070 --> 00:09:06,540
You did something amazing, CEO Baek.

152
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:10,450
Well, then, shall we start the Trunk Show meeting?

153
00:09:10,910 --> 00:09:12,950
We're finally doing this after three months of preparations.

154
00:09:13,780 --> 00:09:14,820
I hope it goes well.

155
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:16,090
Of course it will.

156
00:09:16,150 --> 00:09:18,520
The entire staff poured their souls into it.

157
00:09:19,820 --> 00:09:21,820
You two, when Bruni arrives,

158
00:09:21,890 --> 00:09:24,160
please have the relevant materials ready...

159
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:25,590
so you can answer any requests immediately.

160
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:27,300
Vice President Kang.

161
00:09:27,530 --> 00:09:30,270
Please prepare the VIP list for the Trunk Show.

162
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:32,030
Yes, right away.

163
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:36,270
Director Song, please prepare sample photos of the outfits...

164
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:37,840
for the models on the runway.

165
00:09:39,010 --> 00:09:40,540
And the backup options too, just in case.

166
00:09:41,010 --> 00:09:42,010
Okay.

167
00:09:44,310 --> 00:09:45,950
I'm suddenly nervous.

168
00:09:46,150 --> 00:09:47,550
Of course you should be nervous.

169
00:09:47,850 --> 00:09:49,750
The brand is an icon for every bride and groom,

170
00:09:49,820 --> 00:09:52,490
and we're about to meet Bruni from Bruni & Co. in the flesh.

171
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:53,890
That's right.

172
00:09:54,890 --> 00:09:57,860
For Bruni & Co. to collaborate with us...

173
00:09:58,190 --> 00:10:00,060
is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.

174
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:03,400
So I need everyone to be on their A-game.

175
00:10:04,070 --> 00:10:05,130
- Yes, of course. - Yes.

176
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:08,940
By the way, the venue for the Trunk Show...

177
00:10:09,010 --> 00:10:10,770
hasn't been decided yet, right?

178
00:10:12,410 --> 00:10:14,510
That's something for Bruni's team to decide.

179
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:18,850
Bruni is surprisingly picky about the venue.

180
00:10:20,050 --> 00:10:21,050
Just like someone we know.

181
00:10:23,950 --> 00:10:26,490
CEO Ji, do you have anything to add?

182
00:10:27,990 --> 00:10:30,890
Well, I doubt my opinion is really needed.

183
00:10:31,390 --> 00:10:35,030
I'm sure CEO Baek already has all the answers.

184
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:36,770
So then, CEO Ji,

185
00:10:36,770 --> 00:10:39,840
you have no objections to my decision?

186
00:10:40,670 --> 00:10:42,140
Kim Yu Ju for the finale model.

187
00:10:43,210 --> 00:10:45,070
What? Kim Yu Ju?

188
00:10:45,570 --> 00:10:47,240
I don't care about anything else.

189
00:10:47,310 --> 00:10:49,450
Just let me have my way on that one thing.

190
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:55,220
Well, I'll just step out then...

191
00:10:55,620 --> 00:10:57,420
I should get going too.

192
00:10:57,750 --> 00:10:58,820
Well, then...

193
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:02,990
Did you just say Kim Yu Ju?

194
00:11:03,290 --> 00:11:05,160
Why? Is there a problem?

195
00:11:05,290 --> 00:11:06,800
Of course there's a problem.

196
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:08,330
Kim Yu Ju is the one who bailed on us...

197
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:09,870
on the day of last year's Trunk Show.

198
00:11:10,270 --> 00:11:12,600
Have you already forgotten how much trouble she caused us?

199
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:14,670
She had unavoidable circumstances back then.

200
00:11:14,740 --> 00:11:16,170
It won't happen this year.

201
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:17,610
Unavoidable circumstances?

202
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:19,680
Getting wasted because her boyfriend dumped her,

203
00:11:19,740 --> 00:11:21,180
oversleeping, and then bailing on the show?

204
00:11:21,310 --> 00:11:22,650
You call that unavoidable circumstances?

205
00:11:22,710 --> 00:11:23,710
Forget it.

206
00:11:23,780 --> 00:11:25,410
The finale model has to be Yu Ju.

207
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:28,350
If you really hate that idea, then withdraw the divorce papers.

208
00:11:31,350 --> 00:11:32,660
Are you kidding me right now?

209
00:11:32,690 --> 00:11:34,060
Then are we really getting a divorce?

210
00:11:36,790 --> 00:11:38,560
Forget it. We'll talk later.

211
00:11:39,060 --> 00:11:40,760
My lawyer will be here soon.

212
00:11:41,230 --> 00:11:42,260
"My lawyer?"

213
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:44,330
Why do you have a lawyer? You have a lawyer?

214
00:11:44,330 --> 00:11:45,330
Yes.

215
00:11:47,270 --> 00:11:48,500
There you are.

216
00:11:50,010 --> 00:11:51,140
From now on, CEO Baek...

217
00:11:51,570 --> 00:11:52,910
will be speaking with me.

218
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:01,520
She really was...

219
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:05,320
- a divorce lawyer? - I thought she looked familiar.

220
00:12:05,420 --> 00:12:07,120
She was a client who had a dress fitted at our shop.

221
00:12:07,190 --> 00:12:09,090
From the Exclusive Line, at that.

222
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:10,560
The Exclusive Line?

223
00:12:10,760 --> 00:12:12,960
Doesn't that mean she waited a whole year for your dress?

224
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:14,100
That's what I'm saying.

225
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:15,630
She once said she decided to get married...

226
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:17,370
after seeing my dress. Unbelievable.

227
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:20,200
Anyway, your wife is really something else.

228
00:12:20,670 --> 00:12:22,810
How could she hire a client like that as her lawyer?

229
00:12:22,970 --> 00:12:24,140
Hey, hold on.

230
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:31,110
I was wondering why the complaint was written that way.

231
00:12:31,310 --> 00:12:32,480
It all makes sense now.

232
00:12:32,650 --> 00:12:33,650
(A Fierce Lawyer's Take)

233
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:35,020
(An Easy Guide To Law From A Divorce Lawyer)

234
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:36,350
Once she bites,

235
00:12:36,420 --> 00:12:38,020
she looks like she'll never let go.

236
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:41,260
But what about you?

237
00:12:41,420 --> 00:12:43,890
- So what are you going to do now? - What do you mean, what am I to do?

238
00:12:44,090 --> 00:12:46,600
She's openly bringing a divorce lawyer around now.

239
00:12:47,430 --> 00:12:48,430
Are you really...

240
00:12:48,930 --> 00:12:49,930
getting a divorce?

241
00:13:03,510 --> 00:13:05,510
- Who is it? - My mom.

242
00:13:05,850 --> 00:13:07,780
She told me to come home for a bit on my lunch break.

243
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:10,020
She said a lawyer is coming over.

244
00:13:10,750 --> 00:13:11,750
Well,

245
00:13:12,220 --> 00:13:13,760
I guess you can't just sit back and take it.

246
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,360
This is so frustrating.

247
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:24,570
To have the wedding of a lifetime,

248
00:13:25,070 --> 00:13:27,100
I chose a dress your husband designed.

249
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,270
I'm divorced too, you know.

250
00:13:31,210 --> 00:13:32,270
Come to think of it,

251
00:13:32,540 --> 00:13:34,840
I also got married in a dress my husband designed.

252
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:39,280
But...

253
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:41,380
do you really not have an office?

254
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:44,720
My concept is to provide a personal, mobile service.

255
00:13:45,350 --> 00:13:48,490
Still, it must be tiring to come all the way out here every time.

256
00:13:48,960 --> 00:13:50,590
It was at first,

257
00:13:51,290 --> 00:13:52,860
but now I prefer it.

258
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:55,060
I see much more this way...

259
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:57,000
than I would sitting in an office waiting for clients.

260
00:13:57,400 --> 00:13:59,570
I can see so much more.

261
00:14:01,570 --> 00:14:03,340
Judging by your husband's expression earlier,

262
00:14:03,770 --> 00:14:05,980
he doesn't seem ready for this yet.

263
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:08,510
That's actually what I'm worried about.

264
00:14:09,710 --> 00:14:13,250
I even sent the complaint, but he still doesn't seem to get it.

265
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:17,750
Right after receiving a complaint, it's common to be in denial.

266
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:22,020
He'll hire a lawyer soon and start fighting back,

267
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:24,060
so don't let your guard down.

268
00:14:29,670 --> 00:14:31,230
Is this a joke? She demands 790,000 dollars?

269
00:14:31,970 --> 00:14:34,400
It says here, 790,000 dollars in property division,

270
00:14:34,470 --> 00:14:35,570
plus alimony.

271
00:14:36,810 --> 00:14:39,340
This is absolutely absurd.

272
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:41,740
- Right? - Yes, well...

273
00:14:41,980 --> 00:14:43,950
In my opinion, about...

274
00:14:44,250 --> 00:14:45,250
forty percent.

275
00:14:45,310 --> 00:14:46,320
Excuse me?

276
00:14:46,550 --> 00:14:48,220
Forty percent or half,

277
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:49,550
isn't that pretty much the same thing?

278
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:52,290
Mom, let's just hear the lawyer out first.

279
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:54,190
What about alimony?

280
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:58,230
My son didn't do anything wrong, so we don't have to pay it, do we?

281
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:01,260
That...

282
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,640
remains to be seen.

283
00:15:07,070 --> 00:15:10,340
What does that mean? What remains to be seen?

284
00:15:10,540 --> 00:15:12,410
We hired you to find that out,

285
00:15:12,510 --> 00:15:14,940
but you're being so vague.

286
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:16,580
Mom, why are you only talking about money...

287
00:15:16,650 --> 00:15:18,110
the moment we sit down?

288
00:15:18,180 --> 00:15:20,050
Shouldn't you hear my side of the story first?

289
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:21,980
When it comes to priorities, the money comes first.

290
00:15:22,150 --> 00:15:23,490
Isn't that why we brought him here?

291
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:28,420
The legal fees won't be cheap, either.

292
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:31,190
The legal fees are pretty steep, right?

293
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:34,430
In my case, I require a 15,000-dollar retainer...

294
00:15:35,130 --> 00:15:38,330
and a ten percent success fee.

295
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:41,000
That's the industry standard.

296
00:15:41,340 --> 00:15:43,440
Hold on, 15,000 dollars?

297
00:15:43,970 --> 00:15:47,380
They're the ones who filed suit, so why do I have to pay that?

298
00:15:49,580 --> 00:15:52,350
I'm not doing it. I won't do it.

299
00:15:52,550 --> 00:15:53,580
I'm not doing this.

300
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:56,320
Hey, where do you think you're going?

301
00:15:56,790 --> 00:15:58,590
It was so hard to get him to come here.

302
00:15:58,850 --> 00:15:59,920
Come on, Won Ho.

303
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:01,860
He's supposed to be a top-notch lawyer.

304
00:16:02,090 --> 00:16:04,190
Hey, let's just hear him out. Come back here.

305
00:16:04,530 --> 00:16:05,530
Mom, didn't you hear him?

306
00:16:05,530 --> 00:16:06,960
He said 15,000 dollars.

307
00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:08,930
So you'd rather save that money...

308
00:16:09,030 --> 00:16:11,870
and let that vixen take your entire, hard-earned fortune?

309
00:16:11,930 --> 00:16:13,700
Yes, I'd rather do that.

310
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:15,140
You want me to save money on the settlement...

311
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,840
by giving a lawyer I've never even met...

312
00:16:16,910 --> 00:16:18,270
fifteen thousand dollars?

313
00:16:18,340 --> 00:16:20,940
I'd rather let Baek Mi Young take everything, all right?

314
00:16:21,010 --> 00:16:22,240
This kid is unbelievable.

315
00:16:22,910 --> 00:16:24,110
Hey, Ji Won Ho, you idiot.

316
00:16:25,310 --> 00:16:27,180
My mother's just a little upset, sir.

317
00:16:27,250 --> 00:16:29,890
I'm not doing it. I'm sorry, thank you for coming. You can go.

318
00:16:30,350 --> 00:16:31,350
Hey, you little brat.

319
00:16:46,140 --> 00:16:47,770
Darn it, I'm bleeding.

320
00:16:51,310 --> 00:16:53,010
Get out!

321
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:54,980
Go live however you want, you rotten brat. Get out.

322
00:16:55,040 --> 00:16:58,180
- Get out! - Let go of me. I'm leaving!

323
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:03,250
- Get out. - I'm leaving.

324
00:17:03,250 --> 00:17:04,850
- Get out. - Stop hitting me.

325
00:17:05,790 --> 00:17:06,860
Darn it.

326
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:15,530
What an ordeal. A waste of time.

327
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:17,600
Where have you been?

328
00:17:21,340 --> 00:17:22,470
Do you know what time it is?

329
00:17:24,410 --> 00:17:25,470
It's 3pm. Why?

330
00:17:25,670 --> 00:17:27,510
Did you forget that Bruni is coming soon?

331
00:17:28,410 --> 00:17:29,550
Is that today?

332
00:17:31,750 --> 00:17:35,250
CEO Ji, where have you been? Your clothes are a mess.

333
00:17:35,620 --> 00:17:37,850
- You should get changed. - No, it's fine.

334
00:17:38,050 --> 00:17:39,150
They're here.

335
00:17:58,970 --> 00:18:01,740
Bruni has chosen our Calvin Hotel as the venue...

336
00:18:02,210 --> 00:18:04,210
for the upcoming Trunk Show,

337
00:18:04,650 --> 00:18:06,150
so I've come to see you all today.

338
00:18:06,980 --> 00:18:09,350
So that the collaborative show between J&White and Bruni...

339
00:18:09,550 --> 00:18:11,720
can proceed without any problems,

340
00:18:12,490 --> 00:18:13,660
I will do my absolute best.

341
00:18:15,590 --> 00:18:17,760
Yes. I hope everyone does their best on this Trunk Show...

342
00:18:17,890 --> 00:18:20,300
so we can achieve the best possible results.

343
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:25,470
CEO Baek?

344
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,240
Yes?

345
00:18:28,370 --> 00:18:30,710
Yes. We at J&White...

346
00:18:31,170 --> 00:18:34,080
will prepare the most exquisite dresses...

347
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:36,650
that will best accentuate Bruni's jewellery.

348
00:18:37,350 --> 00:18:41,220
Then I suppose it's my job to find a Cinderella worthy of them.

349
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:43,320
Well,

350
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:45,190
I have one other task I'm in charge of.

351
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:47,860
The model for the finale...

352
00:18:48,220 --> 00:18:50,160
is my responsibility to cast.

353
00:18:53,030 --> 00:18:55,360
For someone in the hotel business, Calvin,

354
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:57,570
you certainly have your hands in a lot of things.

355
00:18:57,800 --> 00:19:00,040
I'm known for being well-connected in this field,

356
00:19:00,570 --> 00:19:02,270
so you can trust me with this.

357
00:19:03,340 --> 00:19:05,070
I'm afraid that will be a problem.

358
00:19:05,910 --> 00:19:09,180
As for the model for the finale, we've already completed the casting.

359
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:12,010
You already did? When?

360
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:15,820
Won Ho, what are you doing?

361
00:19:16,720 --> 00:19:19,590
Have you already forgotten we chose a model?

362
00:19:21,360 --> 00:19:22,990
The model for the finale of this show...

363
00:19:23,430 --> 00:19:24,960
will be Kim Yu Ju.

364
00:19:25,790 --> 00:19:28,200
Ms. Kim is a long time muse...

365
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:31,200
who provides my husband with design inspiration.

366
00:19:31,570 --> 00:19:34,600
So, Kim Yu Ju is your husband's muse.

367
00:19:37,410 --> 00:19:38,710
Then let's proceed with that.

368
00:19:50,220 --> 00:19:51,620
"There is no way I'm working with Kim Yu Ju."

369
00:19:51,690 --> 00:19:52,960
"Absolutely not to Kim Yu Ju."

370
00:19:53,020 --> 00:19:54,820
And now, all of a sudden, she's my "muse?"

371
00:19:55,020 --> 00:19:56,390
Did you eat something bad for lunch?

372
00:19:56,560 --> 00:19:57,730
You're the one who said...

373
00:19:58,060 --> 00:20:01,130
it had to be Kim Yu Ju. That if I didn't use Kim Yu Ju,

374
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,330
I should withdraw the complaint.

375
00:20:03,070 --> 00:20:04,130
Wait, don't tell me...

376
00:20:04,930 --> 00:20:06,870
you only agreed to use Kim Yu Ju because of that?

377
00:20:07,300 --> 00:20:08,300
Of course.

378
00:20:09,070 --> 00:20:10,570
Right. Of course.

379
00:20:11,640 --> 00:20:14,540
But how can you act so natural about it?

380
00:20:15,010 --> 00:20:17,150
- About what? - You and Calvin.

381
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:19,720
As if nothing ever happened between you two.

382
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:21,850
What are you trying to say?

383
00:20:22,350 --> 00:20:24,450
A normal person would feel a little...

384
00:20:24,690 --> 00:20:27,560
uncomfortable and upset. Wouldn't you agree?

385
00:20:28,020 --> 00:20:31,790
How can you smile so naturally? It's unbelievable.

386
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:33,160
Smile? Who was smiling?

387
00:20:33,230 --> 00:20:35,700
Who was smiling? I saw you give him a huge smile.

388
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:38,530
This is your problem.

389
00:20:38,600 --> 00:20:40,140
What's my problem now?

390
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:43,240
Calvin managed to win over Bruni and is expanding his business,

391
00:20:43,370 --> 00:20:45,110
while you're here thinking such pathetic things.

392
00:20:45,870 --> 00:20:47,980
What? Are you comparing me to Calvin right now?

393
00:20:48,410 --> 00:20:50,010
Are you embarrassed by me? Is that it?

394
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:51,110
I am embarrassed.

395
00:20:51,610 --> 00:20:52,750
Just look at yourself.

396
00:20:52,810 --> 00:20:54,450
What do you think Calvin thinks of you?

397
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:56,850
You couldn't even help me save face in front of my ex.

398
00:20:56,920 --> 00:20:58,390
The fact that you're my husband...

399
00:20:58,750 --> 00:21:00,820
is so embarrassing. Happy now?

400
00:21:15,040 --> 00:21:17,170
Isn't Calvin drop-dead gorgeous in person?

401
00:21:17,340 --> 00:21:19,110
I know. He's handsome,

402
00:21:19,110 --> 00:21:20,280
and they say he's super talented too.

403
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:22,140
The Trunk Show is going to be amazing, right?

404
00:21:22,410 --> 00:21:24,510
- Yes. - Of course. It's his hotel.

405
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:27,350
- That's true. - I'm excited thinking about it.

406
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:29,620
Stop chitchatting and let's focus.

407
00:21:29,620 --> 00:21:30,690
- Okay. - Okay.

408
00:21:57,510 --> 00:21:58,780
I told you not to come back.

409
00:21:59,450 --> 00:22:02,020
Why are you suddenly treating me like this?

410
00:22:02,320 --> 00:22:05,620
- Don't do this to me. - I told you, I'm getting married.

411
00:22:07,990 --> 00:22:09,930
I don't want to make you feel any more miserable.

412
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:35,120
Look,

413
00:22:35,980 --> 00:22:38,050
from now on, just pretend you don't know me.

414
00:22:39,250 --> 00:22:40,290
To me,

415
00:22:40,960 --> 00:22:43,330
you are like someone who doesn't exist.

416
00:22:59,570 --> 00:23:02,010
- Yes? - You have a visitor.

417
00:23:02,840 --> 00:23:05,280
- Who is it? - It's Ms. Baek Mi Young.

418
00:23:06,080 --> 00:23:07,180
Show her in.

419
00:23:12,750 --> 00:23:14,860
What brings you here? Have a seat.

420
00:23:15,760 --> 00:23:17,030
Was this part of your plan too?

421
00:23:17,790 --> 00:23:20,260
- What? - The fact that Bruni chose...

422
00:23:20,330 --> 00:23:21,630
the Calvin Hotel for the Trunk Show.

423
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:24,100
That wasn't a coincidence, was it?

424
00:23:24,530 --> 00:23:26,100
I made a strong pitch for it.

425
00:23:27,200 --> 00:23:28,900
I knew you were collaborating with Bruni.

426
00:23:30,910 --> 00:23:31,910
Why?

427
00:23:32,540 --> 00:23:33,710
Because you wanted to see me again?

428
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:38,480
Fine. It doesn't matter.

429
00:23:39,080 --> 00:23:40,980
No matter what you're plotting,

430
00:23:41,550 --> 00:23:43,390
I won't even bat an eye.

431
00:23:44,620 --> 00:23:45,620
But...

432
00:23:46,390 --> 00:23:47,960
please don't cross the line.

433
00:23:49,220 --> 00:23:52,030
The moment you cross that line, be it in business or anything else,

434
00:23:53,530 --> 00:23:55,100
I won't just stand by.

435
00:24:25,990 --> 00:24:27,300
Are you embarrassed by me?

436
00:24:27,600 --> 00:24:29,430
I am embarrassed.

437
00:24:29,660 --> 00:24:31,900
You couldn't even help me save face in front of my ex.

438
00:24:31,970 --> 00:24:33,840
The fact that you're my husband...

439
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:35,400
is so embarrassing.

440
00:24:57,760 --> 00:25:00,400
I think my wife really hates me.

441
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:03,000
If she liked you, would she be asking for a divorce?

442
00:25:04,030 --> 00:25:05,130
What the heck?

443
00:25:05,830 --> 00:25:07,800
Why are you so blunt, Father?

444
00:25:08,200 --> 00:25:10,640
If you're looking for comfort, you should pray.

445
00:25:11,170 --> 00:25:13,480
Find your peace with the Lord.

446
00:25:17,680 --> 00:25:19,010
About that day...

447
00:25:19,210 --> 00:25:21,850
Have you thought about being honest with your wife about it?

448
00:25:23,150 --> 00:25:25,490
- That day? - You know.

449
00:25:26,050 --> 00:25:27,190
Three years ago.

450
00:25:31,460 --> 00:25:34,760
Mi Young, just put that down. Okay? Put it down right now.

451
00:25:34,830 --> 00:25:37,930
- Stop. Don't come any closer. - Put it down.

452
00:25:38,800 --> 00:25:39,800
Darn it.

453
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:43,040
Stop.

454
00:25:43,310 --> 00:25:44,410
Darn it.

455
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:47,780
The way you two ended up...

456
00:25:47,840 --> 00:25:49,510
I wonder if it's because of that.

457
00:25:50,480 --> 00:25:52,080
And if I think about it more,

458
00:25:52,380 --> 00:25:54,120
I start to wonder if it's my fault.

459
00:25:55,080 --> 00:25:58,150
Come on, that's not why. It's not your fault, Father.

460
00:25:58,690 --> 00:25:59,920
Don't think like that.

461
00:26:10,700 --> 00:26:15,140
Prayers are for the Lord, and counselling is for professionals.

462
00:26:23,040 --> 00:26:25,750
(Bae Su Ji, Lawyer, Neighbourhood Law Office)

463
00:26:25,850 --> 00:26:29,480
(Bae Su Ji Law Office)

464
00:26:55,510 --> 00:26:56,680
Excuse me.

465
00:26:59,350 --> 00:27:00,350
Yes?

466
00:27:00,680 --> 00:27:05,050
Hello. I was referred here.

467
00:27:05,220 --> 00:27:06,220
Well...

468
00:27:08,890 --> 00:27:12,530
I'd like to get some advice about a divorce.

469
00:27:12,930 --> 00:27:14,430
You're in the right place.

470
00:27:14,660 --> 00:27:17,600
This firm's been the go-to spot for 30 years.

471
00:27:17,970 --> 00:27:19,430
Thirty years?

472
00:27:20,100 --> 00:27:22,470
So, when did you start working here...

473
00:27:22,540 --> 00:27:24,640
And why are you asking?

474
00:27:25,870 --> 00:27:27,380
What is this, an interrogation?

475
00:27:46,830 --> 00:27:49,530
I like my meat well-done. Is that okay with you?

476
00:27:49,600 --> 00:27:50,730
Yes, of course.

477
00:27:52,630 --> 00:27:53,700
By the way,

478
00:27:54,070 --> 00:27:56,200
is that your real name?

479
00:27:57,740 --> 00:27:58,810
No, it's just...

480
00:27:58,870 --> 00:28:00,380
It's just that when I first heard your name,

481
00:28:00,380 --> 00:28:02,340
I thought you were a young woman.

482
00:28:07,980 --> 00:28:09,480
I used to be a woman.

483
00:28:09,880 --> 00:28:10,890
What?

484
00:28:11,850 --> 00:28:13,020
In my past life.

485
00:28:13,290 --> 00:28:15,290
In your past life...

486
00:28:19,930 --> 00:28:21,260
Father Kwon sent you?

487
00:28:21,700 --> 00:28:24,170
Yes. He said...

488
00:28:24,230 --> 00:28:26,670
you're an expert in divorce cases.

489
00:28:27,670 --> 00:28:28,800
An expert?

490
00:28:35,910 --> 00:28:38,050
I'm a heavyweight in this business.

491
00:28:39,350 --> 00:28:42,320
So, in your past life, you were a woman,

492
00:28:42,320 --> 00:28:44,920
and in this life, you're a heavyweight?

493
00:28:47,390 --> 00:28:48,390
I see.

494
00:28:49,760 --> 00:28:51,290
If you got served anything, let me see it.

495
00:28:53,030 --> 00:28:55,900
- The complaint you were served. - Yes.

496
00:28:59,400 --> 00:29:00,600
(Yeonnam Family Court)

497
00:29:15,350 --> 00:29:16,720
Let's see.

498
00:29:21,590 --> 00:29:23,530
The grounds for divorce are...

499
00:29:24,630 --> 00:29:28,030
- Verbal abuse, assault, contempt... - Excuse me, sir.

500
00:29:28,430 --> 00:29:30,060
Could you please keep your voice down?

501
00:29:31,770 --> 00:29:33,500
So you have the decency to be embarrassed.

502
00:29:35,340 --> 00:29:36,800
Seven hundred ninety thousand is a bargain.

503
00:29:37,810 --> 00:29:38,810
What?

504
00:29:39,040 --> 00:29:41,380
If all this is true, then 790,000 dollars is a bargain.

505
00:29:43,650 --> 00:29:46,950
You know, you sound just like a real estate agent.

506
00:29:47,020 --> 00:29:48,920
I'm not here to sell a house.

507
00:29:51,950 --> 00:29:52,950
From the looks of you,

508
00:29:53,020 --> 00:29:54,890
she could've ripped you off for a million dollars.

509
00:29:55,520 --> 00:29:57,230
Your wife is going easy on you.

510
00:29:57,430 --> 00:30:00,600
Rip me off? What am I, a Band-Aid?

511
00:30:00,730 --> 00:30:04,670
- Pay up. - Pay up? I can't listen anymore.

512
00:30:05,100 --> 00:30:06,130
Listen here.

513
00:30:06,470 --> 00:30:08,500
I have nothing more to say to someone...

514
00:30:08,570 --> 00:30:10,270
who is so disrespectful.

515
00:30:10,870 --> 00:30:13,040
- Disrespectful? - Yes, disrespectful.

516
00:30:14,310 --> 00:30:17,710
- Abuse, profanity, assault. - What do you think you're doing?

517
00:30:17,780 --> 00:30:19,350
What, you deny it?

518
00:30:20,520 --> 00:30:22,050
Then how about this?

519
00:30:22,520 --> 00:30:24,890
- Refusal of sexual relations. - Hey, give that to me.

520
00:30:25,020 --> 00:30:26,390
Give it to me, now!

521
00:30:29,420 --> 00:30:32,130
Know your enemy and know yourself.

522
00:30:33,290 --> 00:30:35,960
First, you need to understand yourself.

523
00:30:36,830 --> 00:30:39,830
It means admitting that your mess is, in fact, a mess.

524
00:30:39,830 --> 00:30:42,100
That's where the fight begins.

525
00:30:43,170 --> 00:30:44,910
Come back when you're ready for a divorce.

526
00:30:44,970 --> 00:30:46,340
We'll talk then.

527
00:31:09,300 --> 00:31:10,300
But...

528
00:31:10,930 --> 00:31:12,630
please don't cross the line.

529
00:31:13,530 --> 00:31:14,940
The moment you cross that line,

530
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:16,670
be it in business or anything else,

531
00:31:18,110 --> 00:31:19,740
I won't just stand by.

532
00:31:32,720 --> 00:31:34,560
The model for the finale of this show...

533
00:31:34,820 --> 00:31:36,520
will be Kim Yu Ju.

534
00:31:37,260 --> 00:31:39,730
Ms. Kim is a long time muse...

535
00:31:39,960 --> 00:31:42,900
who provides my husband with design inspiration.

536
00:31:56,440 --> 00:31:57,450
Secretary Han.

537
00:31:57,980 --> 00:31:59,450
Do some digging on Kim Yu Ju for me.

538
00:32:01,420 --> 00:32:03,920
This show really all depends on you, Yu Ju.

539
00:32:04,490 --> 00:32:05,590
If you do well,

540
00:32:05,650 --> 00:32:07,090
you'll save the show and me along with it.

541
00:32:07,490 --> 00:32:10,790
I'm not just saying that. I'm counting on you.

542
00:32:12,230 --> 00:32:13,730
And...

543
00:32:13,800 --> 00:32:16,660
are you and your boyfriend getting along these days?

544
00:32:17,700 --> 00:32:21,070
Oh, you're single. Then I have nothing to worry about.

545
00:32:21,640 --> 00:32:23,040
All right. I'll see you then.

546
00:32:23,570 --> 00:32:24,940
Yes, take care.

547
00:32:25,470 --> 00:32:26,470
Yes.

548
00:32:29,780 --> 00:32:32,450
Hey. Aren't you overdoing it?

549
00:32:32,850 --> 00:32:34,850
The whole show depends on Kim Yu Ju?

550
00:32:35,050 --> 00:32:37,390
Of course I'm overdoing it. But I have to lay it on thick...

551
00:32:37,390 --> 00:32:38,920
so she feels the pressure.

552
00:32:39,420 --> 00:32:41,990
If this show gets ruined because of Yu Ju again,

553
00:32:42,060 --> 00:32:43,830
Baek Mi Young might actually divorce me.

554
00:32:44,490 --> 00:32:47,760
Is this Trunk Show really that important to you?

555
00:32:47,830 --> 00:32:50,500
I'm going to make this show a huge success...

556
00:32:50,570 --> 00:32:52,130
to win Mi Young's heart back...

557
00:32:52,200 --> 00:32:54,340
and completely crush that jerk Calvin.

558
00:32:54,640 --> 00:32:56,500
So he'll never even think of coming near Mi Young again.

559
00:32:57,110 --> 00:32:58,110
But...

560
00:32:58,610 --> 00:33:00,880
I don't think it's going to be that simple.

561
00:33:02,280 --> 00:33:05,050
- What? - I'm talking about Kim Yu Ju.

562
00:33:05,610 --> 00:33:07,820
She already has a history of flaking on a show,

563
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:10,490
so it's a bit risky to just trust her blindly.

564
00:33:11,150 --> 00:33:13,390
That's true. But what can I do?

565
00:33:15,920 --> 00:33:18,690
Then, should I go pick her up myself?

566
00:33:19,860 --> 00:33:21,300
You're going to pick her up?

567
00:33:21,630 --> 00:33:24,000
The moment Kim Yu Ju wakes up on the day of the show,

568
00:33:24,070 --> 00:33:25,470
I'll pick her up and bring her right over.

569
00:33:25,970 --> 00:33:28,170
Hey, that would work.

570
00:33:28,300 --> 00:33:30,300
That's our Kyung Tae, always thinking.

571
00:33:31,310 --> 00:33:33,240
Hey, hurry up and look at this so we can go get some noodles.

572
00:33:33,410 --> 00:33:34,410
Okay.

573
00:33:34,840 --> 00:33:36,510
Oh, there's a lot of new stuff.

574
00:33:38,980 --> 00:33:40,210
Hello.

575
00:33:40,380 --> 00:33:43,050
- It's been a while. - It's good to see you.

576
00:33:43,180 --> 00:33:44,190
Welcome.

577
00:33:44,490 --> 00:33:46,520
I'm sorry about last year.

578
00:33:46,820 --> 00:33:49,390
I felt terrible after bailing on the show.

579
00:33:49,520 --> 00:33:52,260
You have to keep your promise this time.

580
00:33:52,360 --> 00:33:53,460
Of course.

581
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:57,200
By the way, CEO Ji was right.

582
00:33:57,830 --> 00:33:59,470
- He was? - When he first called...

583
00:33:59,470 --> 00:34:01,100
to offer me the job,

584
00:34:01,440 --> 00:34:03,600
he said that his wife and I...

585
00:34:03,670 --> 00:34:05,710
have a very similar vibe.

586
00:34:06,410 --> 00:34:08,710
That's why he said he had his eyes on me.

587
00:34:12,180 --> 00:34:13,850
Oh, that's true.

588
00:34:14,150 --> 00:34:16,720
Now that I see you two, she looks just like you did...

589
00:34:16,780 --> 00:34:18,420
when you were younger, CEO Baek.

590
00:34:19,020 --> 00:34:21,190
So, what should I start with?

591
00:34:21,260 --> 00:34:23,260
First, should we get your measurements?

592
00:34:23,320 --> 00:34:24,330
Come this way.

593
00:35:02,400 --> 00:35:04,700
Oh, come on. What is it?

594
00:35:05,100 --> 00:35:06,600
Just wait a second.

595
00:35:07,130 --> 00:35:08,440
Seriously.

596
00:35:11,810 --> 00:35:15,980
- Yes? - Open your eyes when I say three.

597
00:35:16,710 --> 00:35:18,650
Okay. Hurry up.

598
00:35:19,610 --> 00:35:22,220
One, two.

599
00:35:22,320 --> 00:35:23,450
three.

600
00:35:36,960 --> 00:35:38,100
What do you think?

601
00:35:47,680 --> 00:35:49,080
Are you surprised?

602
00:35:51,250 --> 00:35:52,250
Yes.

603
00:35:55,080 --> 00:35:57,590
This is my first piece.

604
00:35:58,250 --> 00:36:00,050
It's still a bit rough, isn't it?

605
00:36:00,490 --> 00:36:01,790
No.

606
00:36:02,860 --> 00:36:04,260
It's so beautiful.

607
00:36:07,460 --> 00:36:09,060
Mi Young, then...

608
00:36:11,130 --> 00:36:12,370
will you wear this...

609
00:36:14,040 --> 00:36:15,740
and walk with me?

610
00:36:20,340 --> 00:36:21,480
Will you...

611
00:36:22,810 --> 00:36:24,110
marry me?

612
00:37:13,530 --> 00:37:16,800
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

613
00:37:21,340 --> 00:37:23,500
When he first called to offer me the job,

614
00:37:24,040 --> 00:37:28,180
he said that his wife and I have a very similar vibe.

615
00:37:33,250 --> 00:37:35,220
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

616
00:37:45,430 --> 00:37:46,430
CEO Baek.

617
00:37:50,060 --> 00:37:51,170
What did you think of Kim Yu Ju?

618
00:37:53,500 --> 00:37:56,340
What style do you think suits Kim Yu Ju best?

619
00:37:56,940 --> 00:37:58,440
She looked good in pretty much everything.

620
00:37:58,770 --> 00:37:59,910
Probably because she's a good model.

621
00:38:00,810 --> 00:38:02,440
What? You're always so indecisive.

622
00:38:03,580 --> 00:38:04,750
Anyway, discuss it with Director Song...

623
00:38:04,810 --> 00:38:05,810
and give me your feedback.

624
00:38:06,580 --> 00:38:08,820
The finale dress has to be finished by this weekend.

625
00:38:10,320 --> 00:38:11,490
It was because of Calvin.

626
00:38:13,120 --> 00:38:14,120
What?

627
00:38:17,630 --> 00:38:19,130
I pushed for Kim Yu Ju,

628
00:38:20,030 --> 00:38:23,100
not because of you, but because of Calvin.

629
00:38:24,400 --> 00:38:25,900
Because I didn't want to lose to him.

630
00:38:27,800 --> 00:38:28,800
No, but...

631
00:38:29,770 --> 00:38:31,810
why are you telling me this now?

632
00:38:33,670 --> 00:38:35,040
I want this Trunk Show...

633
00:38:36,340 --> 00:38:38,110
to be a success to prove a point.

634
00:38:42,850 --> 00:38:44,420
Separate from our relationship,

635
00:38:45,290 --> 00:38:47,290
J&White, which we built together,

636
00:38:48,090 --> 00:38:49,660
I want to prove myself properly.

637
00:38:50,760 --> 00:38:53,430
Okay, I know what you mean.

638
00:38:54,500 --> 00:38:56,330
I'll finish the dress without any setbacks,

639
00:38:56,400 --> 00:38:57,400
so don't worry.

640
00:38:59,070 --> 00:39:01,800
Let's work together to make this Trunk Show a success.

641
00:39:04,470 --> 00:39:05,510
So, as you can see,

642
00:39:05,570 --> 00:39:08,280
it continues into this off-the-shoulder dress...

643
00:39:08,540 --> 00:39:10,850
We brighten the tone with glamorous jewellery.

644
00:39:16,620 --> 00:39:20,050
And this part is the most important, so please pay close attention.

645
00:39:22,690 --> 00:39:24,160
Okay, just one thing now...

646
00:39:24,230 --> 00:39:26,890
That way, the jewellery can be seen from a distance.

647
00:39:27,130 --> 00:39:28,930
Something new here...

648
00:39:29,200 --> 00:39:30,400
Yes, we'll get started.

649
00:39:43,740 --> 00:39:44,750
This looks good.

650
00:39:45,610 --> 00:39:48,420
Start with the beige one, please.

651
00:39:54,690 --> 00:39:58,690
But how did you come up with that idea?

652
00:39:59,430 --> 00:40:01,430
- What? - The finale dress.

653
00:40:02,360 --> 00:40:04,900
It's an homage to the dress I wore at our wedding.

654
00:40:05,670 --> 00:40:07,870
An homage to the dress you wore at our wedding?

655
00:40:10,070 --> 00:40:11,070
Isn't it?

656
00:40:12,210 --> 00:40:13,210
The sketch...

657
00:40:14,110 --> 00:40:16,380
looked almost identical to my wedding dress.

658
00:40:16,640 --> 00:40:18,850
Oh, that kind of design is common.

659
00:40:18,950 --> 00:40:21,050
It's simple, pure, and has no frills.

660
00:40:23,650 --> 00:40:25,290
Then what about Kim Yu Ju?

661
00:40:25,620 --> 00:40:27,020
Why did you decide to work with Kim Yu Ju again?

662
00:40:27,520 --> 00:40:29,660
She's the one who contacted me first.

663
00:40:30,090 --> 00:40:32,160
She said she was very sorry for the mistake she made last year.

664
00:40:32,460 --> 00:40:34,530
She wanted to make up for it this year or something.

665
00:40:35,200 --> 00:40:37,700
So I gave her a special opportunity.

666
00:40:37,930 --> 00:40:39,470
We even agreed to half her usual fee,

667
00:40:39,530 --> 00:40:41,900
so it all worked out. Good move, right?

668
00:40:47,240 --> 00:40:49,010
Honestly, "personality differences" is a bit much, don't you think?

669
00:40:49,480 --> 00:40:50,480
What?

670
00:40:50,740 --> 00:40:53,380
You wrote "personality differences" in the complaint.

671
00:40:53,910 --> 00:40:55,150
But look at today, for example.

672
00:40:55,220 --> 00:40:56,550
Did we really have anything to fight about?

673
00:40:56,820 --> 00:40:59,550
As long as we don't bring up the divorce, we get along just fine.

674
00:41:00,750 --> 00:41:04,060
Or maybe we're just being peaceful because we're at the Pigeon Market.

675
00:41:04,260 --> 00:41:06,590
You know, since pigeons are a symbol of peace.

676
00:41:11,970 --> 00:41:12,970
You think that's funny?

677
00:41:13,670 --> 00:41:14,670
You don't think it's funny?

678
00:41:17,400 --> 00:41:19,510
This is exactly what I mean by "personality differences."

679
00:41:21,040 --> 00:41:22,910
What about this is suddenly "personality differences"?

680
00:41:23,310 --> 00:41:25,780
I've suddenly lost my appetite.

681
00:41:26,710 --> 00:41:28,050
Ma'am, the check, please.

682
00:41:28,350 --> 00:41:30,180
Hey, where are you going? We're not done eating.

683
00:41:30,750 --> 00:41:31,750
None of your business.

684
00:41:32,620 --> 00:41:33,720
Hey, wait up.

685
00:41:38,130 --> 00:41:40,130
She's like a bomb just waiting to go off.

686
00:41:41,000 --> 00:41:43,630
I have no idea when, where, or how she'll explode.

687
00:41:43,700 --> 00:41:45,230
I tried so hard to be accommodating.

688
00:41:45,300 --> 00:41:47,130
Was that really something to blow up about?

689
00:41:47,370 --> 00:41:48,940
You two are at war right now.

690
00:41:49,470 --> 00:41:50,770
In a war, no one warns you...

691
00:41:50,770 --> 00:41:54,910
three seconds before a bomb goes off, saying, "Watch out."

692
00:41:55,310 --> 00:41:57,510
You just have to accept reality.

693
00:41:57,650 --> 00:42:00,510
But did I start this war?

694
00:42:00,710 --> 00:42:02,120
She filed the complaint whenever she felt like it,

695
00:42:02,220 --> 00:42:04,350
and now she attacks me over every little thing I say.

696
00:42:05,420 --> 00:42:07,590
But she has no problem smiling at some other guy.

697
00:42:07,920 --> 00:42:09,290
What other guy?

698
00:42:09,620 --> 00:42:10,990
There's this one jerk.

699
00:42:11,590 --> 00:42:15,360
So she smiles at this jerk,

700
00:42:16,500 --> 00:42:17,830
but she's out for your blood?

701
00:42:18,070 --> 00:42:20,000
Yes, she's out for my blood.

702
00:42:20,070 --> 00:42:21,500
And I don't even know what I did wrong.

703
00:42:25,540 --> 00:42:26,540
I can't let this go.

704
00:42:27,440 --> 00:42:29,380
I need to get to the bottom of this.

705
00:42:30,110 --> 00:42:31,110
Won Ho.

706
00:42:31,410 --> 00:42:32,410
Won Ho.

707
00:42:41,490 --> 00:42:43,920
We're like oil and water.

708
00:42:45,860 --> 00:42:48,200
Just when I think I'm starting to soften up,

709
00:42:49,100 --> 00:42:50,700
we'll say a few words to each other,

710
00:42:51,200 --> 00:42:53,100
and before I know it, we're at each other's throats.

711
00:42:53,630 --> 00:42:55,670
The two of you are on such different wavelengths...

712
00:42:56,340 --> 00:42:57,670
that it's brought you to this point.

713
00:42:58,510 --> 00:42:59,510
Exactly.

714
00:43:00,040 --> 00:43:01,910
That's why I skipped trying for an uncontested divorce...

715
00:43:02,580 --> 00:43:04,110
and went straight for the lawsuit.

716
00:43:04,310 --> 00:43:05,710
I knew we'd never be able to agree on anything.

717
00:43:06,410 --> 00:43:09,950
Were you guys unable to communicate...

718
00:43:10,750 --> 00:43:11,920
that it led to what happened that day?

719
00:43:13,390 --> 00:43:14,420
That day?

720
00:43:15,190 --> 00:43:16,190
That day.

721
00:43:16,720 --> 00:43:19,930
The day of your suicide attempt.

722
00:43:28,300 --> 00:43:29,300
Don't come any closer.

723
00:43:29,570 --> 00:43:30,800
Mi Young, just put that down.

724
00:43:31,140 --> 00:43:32,870
- Don't come any closer. - Put it down.

725
00:43:36,110 --> 00:43:37,240
I said let go.

726
00:43:39,250 --> 00:43:40,780
Please, ma'am.

727
00:43:40,850 --> 00:43:43,520
- Mom, we have guests inside. - And what does that matter?

728
00:43:43,580 --> 00:43:45,090
I'm what's most important. Out of my way. Move.

729
00:43:45,150 --> 00:43:46,150
No, ma'am, please.

730
00:43:46,220 --> 00:43:47,860
That's enough. Come out. I said that's enough.

731
00:43:47,890 --> 00:43:49,560
Where is she? Come out.

732
00:43:49,620 --> 00:43:50,620
Ma'am, please, just a moment.

733
00:43:50,690 --> 00:43:51,990
- Ma'am, she's... - Where is she?

734
00:43:52,260 --> 00:43:53,260
Oh, dear.

735
00:43:53,860 --> 00:43:54,860
Mother.

736
00:43:56,630 --> 00:43:58,270
She's my mother-in-law.

737
00:43:59,000 --> 00:44:02,840
- Ma'am, please calm down. - Mom.

738
00:44:02,900 --> 00:44:04,000
I said let go.

739
00:44:04,840 --> 00:44:06,040
I'm so sorry, Mi Young.

740
00:44:06,140 --> 00:44:07,470
I tried my best to stop her.

741
00:44:08,040 --> 00:44:11,180
Are you really going to go through with a lawsuit against Won Ho?

742
00:44:12,680 --> 00:44:15,050
Answer me. Yes or no?

743
00:44:16,150 --> 00:44:17,150
So it's true?

744
00:44:19,750 --> 00:44:21,660
Ma'am, please, have a seat...

745
00:44:21,720 --> 00:44:22,720
You stay out of this.

746
00:44:23,960 --> 00:44:25,690
Is what you wrote in the complaint really true?

747
00:44:26,960 --> 00:44:29,560
I'm asking if you really meant what you wrote.

748
00:44:33,370 --> 00:44:34,370
Tell me.

749
00:44:35,340 --> 00:44:37,810
What was your real reason for filing the complaint?

750
00:44:38,740 --> 00:44:39,740
That would be me.

751
00:44:41,040 --> 00:44:42,910
I'm the one who sent the complaint.

752
00:44:43,410 --> 00:44:44,410
And who are you?

753
00:44:44,750 --> 00:44:46,780
I'm Baek Mi Young's divorce attorney,

754
00:44:48,320 --> 00:44:49,350
Jeon Chi Hyun.

755
00:44:50,980 --> 00:44:51,990
So you're the one?

756
00:44:52,250 --> 00:44:53,850
You're the one who spouted all that nonsense?

757
00:44:54,120 --> 00:44:56,090
If you have an objection to the contents of the complaint,

758
00:44:56,260 --> 00:44:57,890
please prepare a formal response and submit it.

759
00:44:57,960 --> 00:44:59,960
There's no need to trouble yourself by coming here in person.

760
00:45:00,360 --> 00:45:01,360
What?

761
00:45:02,130 --> 00:45:03,530
A consultation will be difficult today.

762
00:45:04,260 --> 00:45:05,300
I'll come back another time.

763
00:45:06,030 --> 00:45:08,040
Hey. Get back here!

764
00:45:09,140 --> 00:45:10,270
- Mom. - That woman...

765
00:45:10,340 --> 00:45:11,340
What are you doing?

766
00:45:14,010 --> 00:45:16,010
- Ma'am, please stop! - Mom!

767
00:45:19,110 --> 00:45:20,950
You've got some nerve.

768
00:45:21,750 --> 00:45:23,220
Mom.

769
00:45:24,890 --> 00:45:26,890
- Mom, stop. - Let go!

770
00:45:27,520 --> 00:45:28,920
- Mi Young. - Mom.

771
00:45:30,090 --> 00:45:31,130
Who do you think you are?

772
00:45:31,830 --> 00:45:33,690
- What do you know about it? - No, you can't.

773
00:45:33,760 --> 00:45:35,230
- What do you know? - Ma'am.

774
00:45:35,300 --> 00:45:36,530
What do you know?

775
00:45:41,400 --> 00:45:42,400
Mom.

776
00:45:44,940 --> 00:45:46,340
Let go of her hair. Mom.

777
00:45:48,210 --> 00:45:51,580
- Ma'am, please, let her go. - So what if you're a lawyer?

778
00:45:53,850 --> 00:45:56,080
- Ma'am, please let go. - Let go. Let her go, Mom.

779
00:45:56,150 --> 00:45:57,350
What? What was that?

780
00:46:17,170 --> 00:46:18,170
Who do you think you are?

781
00:46:21,740 --> 00:46:24,780
Mi Young, you're making me a birthday dinner yourself?

782
00:46:25,050 --> 00:46:27,380
It's nothing fancy, but I brought a few things.

783
00:46:27,610 --> 00:46:29,650
Mi Young, let me help you cook...

784
00:46:30,820 --> 00:46:32,820
What are you thinking, with your bad back?

785
00:46:33,020 --> 00:46:36,220
Don't. You need to be in good shape to have a baby.

786
00:46:36,720 --> 00:46:39,230
A man can have children until the day he dies.

787
00:46:39,830 --> 00:46:40,830
But a woman...

788
00:46:42,200 --> 00:46:43,400
You know what I mean, right?

789
00:46:44,300 --> 00:46:46,030
Mi Young, did you tell Won Ho...

790
00:46:46,200 --> 00:46:48,140
that you can't get pregnant because I'm stressing you out?

791
00:46:48,470 --> 00:46:50,140
- What? - Why would he say...

792
00:46:50,140 --> 00:46:51,770
something like that if you didn't?

793
00:46:53,840 --> 00:46:55,410
I think I'm finally starting to understand.

794
00:46:57,410 --> 00:46:59,610
After I received the complaint, I felt so wronged the whole time.

795
00:47:01,820 --> 00:47:03,520
I kept wondering why this was happening to me.

796
00:47:05,050 --> 00:47:06,920
What could I have possibly done so wrong?

797
00:47:10,760 --> 00:47:12,060
But when I actually...

798
00:47:13,290 --> 00:47:14,900
saw it with my own eyes,

799
00:47:16,660 --> 00:47:18,400
it all became clear in an instant.

800
00:47:22,970 --> 00:47:25,010
If that's the reality of marriage,

801
00:47:27,340 --> 00:47:29,880
then maybe divorce is the answer.

802
00:47:35,920 --> 00:47:36,920
So?

803
00:47:40,720 --> 00:47:41,920
I'm just going to accept it.

804
00:47:44,160 --> 00:47:45,190
The mess I made...

805
00:47:48,600 --> 00:47:49,700
is, in fact, a mess.

806
00:47:51,970 --> 00:47:53,370
You've come a long way.

807
00:47:54,870 --> 00:47:57,500
So I'm going to give her what she wants, as much as I can.

808
00:47:59,070 --> 00:48:01,480
I'll give my wife everything she wants,

809
00:48:03,280 --> 00:48:05,550
and end things cleanly.

810
00:48:08,420 --> 00:48:09,520
Are you sure you won't regret this?

811
00:48:11,450 --> 00:48:12,450
Yes.

812
00:48:13,190 --> 00:48:14,190
I won't regret it.

813
00:48:14,520 --> 00:48:15,520
Really?

814
00:48:20,530 --> 00:48:21,530
All right.

815
00:48:22,100 --> 00:48:23,130
Good.

816
00:48:24,430 --> 00:48:26,100
Then let's move forward.

817
00:48:43,173 --> 00:48:46,313
Are you really going to go through with a lawsuit against Won Ho?

818
00:48:47,190 --> 00:48:49,360
Answer me. Yes or no?

819
00:48:50,220 --> 00:48:51,220
Are you happy?

820
00:48:53,190 --> 00:48:54,190
Are you?

821
00:48:58,400 --> 00:48:59,400
Are you...

822
00:49:01,230 --> 00:49:02,400
living a good life?

823
00:49:03,970 --> 00:49:04,970
We're like...

824
00:49:05,470 --> 00:49:07,010
oil and water.

825
00:49:08,740 --> 00:49:11,080
Just when I think I'm starting to soften up,

826
00:49:11,950 --> 00:49:13,710
we'll say a few words to each other,

827
00:49:14,080 --> 00:49:16,050
and before I know it, we're at each other's throats.

828
00:49:16,780 --> 00:49:18,850
The two of you are on such different wavelengths...

829
00:49:19,490 --> 00:49:20,850
that it's brought you to this point.

830
00:49:21,690 --> 00:49:24,620
Even if all my dreams came true right now,

831
00:49:25,630 --> 00:49:28,460
I'm sure I'd just develop a new longing.

832
00:49:30,260 --> 00:49:32,300
I want to go further,

833
00:49:32,770 --> 00:49:34,970
all the way to the finish line.

834
00:49:36,500 --> 00:49:37,870
I want this trunk show...

835
00:49:39,010 --> 00:49:40,840
to be a success to prove a point.

836
00:49:41,880 --> 00:49:43,440
Separate from our relationship,

837
00:49:44,340 --> 00:49:46,410
J&White, which we built together,

838
00:49:47,150 --> 00:49:48,850
I want to prove myself properly.

839
00:50:22,880 --> 00:50:23,880
Today...

840
00:50:27,790 --> 00:50:30,520
Mi Young, we'll go wait in the car.

841
00:50:39,930 --> 00:50:40,930
What brings you here?

842
00:50:41,700 --> 00:50:42,840
I came to show my support.

843
00:50:43,870 --> 00:50:44,870
To wish you luck on the show today.

844
00:50:47,340 --> 00:50:48,340
I'll do my best.

845
00:50:49,040 --> 00:50:50,040
Is that all?

846
00:50:50,980 --> 00:50:52,380
If there's anything I can do to help,

847
00:50:52,450 --> 00:50:53,510
just say the word, Mi Young.

848
00:50:54,510 --> 00:50:55,880
All you have to do is ask,

849
00:50:57,080 --> 00:50:58,420
and I can solve anything for you.

850
00:50:59,450 --> 00:51:01,320
You're as confident as ever.

851
00:51:02,460 --> 00:51:03,660
I'm sorry, Calvin.

852
00:51:04,520 --> 00:51:06,560
But I'd rather work hard and fail on my own...

853
00:51:06,830 --> 00:51:08,930
than have you solve my problems for me.

854
00:51:10,130 --> 00:51:11,200
So...

855
00:51:11,630 --> 00:51:13,100
please, don't cross the line.

856
00:51:14,370 --> 00:51:16,070
And don't just show up unannounced like this.

857
00:51:26,280 --> 00:51:27,610
- Over here, please. - Here?

858
00:51:27,680 --> 00:51:30,180
- Look this way, please. - Yes, great.

859
00:51:30,520 --> 00:51:31,520
Yes.

860
00:51:40,490 --> 00:51:42,430
- Good morning, Bruni. - Good morning.

861
00:51:42,530 --> 00:51:44,400
Everything okay?

862
00:51:44,600 --> 00:51:45,600
Yes.

863
00:51:59,480 --> 00:52:00,480
Mr. Ji?

864
00:52:07,020 --> 00:52:08,620
You look really great today.

865
00:52:08,820 --> 00:52:09,960
Oh, what's all this?

866
00:52:10,760 --> 00:52:12,130
What are you doing here?

867
00:52:12,530 --> 00:52:15,600
I'm here for work. I work for the Calvin Hotel now.

868
00:52:15,860 --> 00:52:17,600
I'm here to take pictures for today's show.

869
00:52:23,700 --> 00:52:25,310
I didn't get a chance to say this last time...

870
00:52:25,370 --> 00:52:26,510
because things were so chaotic.

871
00:52:28,140 --> 00:52:29,980
Don't. You don't have a chance.

872
00:52:30,980 --> 00:52:33,480
- Excuse me? - Don't like me.

873
00:52:35,580 --> 00:52:36,620
By any chance,

874
00:52:37,080 --> 00:52:38,690
is there someone you like?

875
00:52:39,920 --> 00:52:40,920
What?

876
00:52:42,620 --> 00:52:43,620
CEO Ji.

877
00:52:44,360 --> 00:52:45,560
Oh, yes, I'm coming.

878
00:52:46,830 --> 00:52:49,030
Anyway, I've made myself clear.

879
00:52:54,100 --> 00:52:55,100
You're here early.

880
00:52:57,000 --> 00:52:58,000
Great atmosphere, right?

881
00:53:16,720 --> 00:53:18,690
Yes, check them one by one with a long ruler.

882
00:53:18,760 --> 00:53:19,760
Yes, got it.

883
00:53:19,830 --> 00:53:21,060
Please hurry.

884
00:53:22,430 --> 00:53:24,330
Excuse me, coming through. Sorry, excuse me.

885
00:53:25,600 --> 00:53:26,900
These aren't the right earrings.

886
00:53:27,670 --> 00:53:28,670
Just a moment.

887
00:53:30,570 --> 00:53:31,740
Yes, Vice President Kang,

888
00:53:31,940 --> 00:53:34,310
you're picking up Kim Yu Ju and are on your way now, right?

889
00:53:35,080 --> 00:53:37,640
Yes, CEO Baek. I've just arrived.

890
00:53:38,780 --> 00:53:39,780
Yes.

891
00:53:39,910 --> 00:53:42,180
If there's no traffic, I think we'll get there a bit early.

892
00:53:44,780 --> 00:53:45,790
What?

893
00:53:46,120 --> 00:53:47,120
Room 301?

894
00:53:48,120 --> 00:53:49,560
CEO Baek, just a moment.

895
00:53:50,720 --> 00:53:53,060
Mr. Kang?

896
00:53:56,100 --> 00:53:57,100
Yu Ju.

897
00:53:58,060 --> 00:53:59,070
Yu Ju?

898
00:53:59,800 --> 00:54:00,800
Are you in there?

899
00:54:02,070 --> 00:54:03,070
Yu Ju.

900
00:54:06,240 --> 00:54:07,240
Yu Ju.

901
00:54:09,740 --> 00:54:10,740
Yu Ju.

902
00:54:12,310 --> 00:54:13,310
Yu Ju.

903
00:54:13,510 --> 00:54:15,720
Are you okay? Yu Ju.

904
00:54:17,520 --> 00:54:19,550
Yu Ju, please wake up.

905
00:54:20,220 --> 00:54:21,220
Yu Ju.

906
00:54:21,450 --> 00:54:22,490
Yu Ju.

907
00:54:31,000 --> 00:54:33,000
I'm really looking forward to today's show.

908
00:54:34,200 --> 00:54:35,270
Me too.

909
00:54:35,340 --> 00:54:36,870
It's truly an honour to be collaborating with you.

910
00:54:37,340 --> 00:54:39,440
Oh, your Italian is quite fluent.

911
00:54:39,610 --> 00:54:41,680
Yes, I studied in Milan for a short time.

912
00:54:41,880 --> 00:54:42,880
Milan?

913
00:54:43,540 --> 00:54:45,750
I see. What a nice surprise.

914
00:54:45,850 --> 00:54:46,850
Thank you.

915
00:54:53,650 --> 00:54:57,320
What? The finale model isn't here yet?

916
00:54:58,120 --> 00:54:59,360
What's going on?

917
00:55:07,170 --> 00:55:08,400
How could this happen?

918
00:55:09,400 --> 00:55:11,200
So, what are Yu Ju's injuries exactly?

919
00:55:11,270 --> 00:55:12,340
How badly is she hurt?

920
00:55:12,540 --> 00:55:13,670
Vice President Kang is with Yu Ju now.

921
00:55:13,740 --> 00:55:16,210
He called an ambulance and is on the way to the hospital with her.

922
00:55:16,740 --> 00:55:19,550
He said it looks like her leg is broken.

923
00:55:21,350 --> 00:55:22,380
What do we do?

924
00:55:22,620 --> 00:55:26,220
Thank goodness the vice president found her when he did.

925
00:55:26,590 --> 00:55:28,050
She'll be fine once she gets treatment.

926
00:55:29,220 --> 00:55:32,030
Right. Yu Ju will be fine.

927
00:55:32,460 --> 00:55:33,590
What about our show?

928
00:55:34,590 --> 00:55:36,600
What do you mean Yu Ju isn't here yet?

929
00:55:36,700 --> 00:55:38,770
Yu Ju got hurt, so she can't make it.

930
00:55:39,300 --> 00:55:41,100
She's on her way to the hospital with the vice president now.

931
00:55:42,270 --> 00:55:43,270
Darn it.

932
00:55:43,940 --> 00:55:44,940
Then...

933
00:55:45,210 --> 00:55:47,840
who's going to walk in the finale?

934
00:55:49,280 --> 00:55:50,540
We'll have to get someone else.

935
00:55:50,610 --> 00:55:51,880
We can't just stand here and do nothing.

936
00:55:52,750 --> 00:55:55,450
Director Song, you have that list of available models, right?

937
00:55:55,920 --> 00:55:56,920
Yes.

938
00:55:56,920 --> 00:55:59,220
Let's call every single model on that list.

939
00:55:59,990 --> 00:56:02,460
We'll be able to find one model who can walk the finale.

940
00:56:03,320 --> 00:56:04,360
I'm counting on you.

941
00:56:04,660 --> 00:56:05,730
Yes, got it.

942
00:56:16,000 --> 00:56:17,570
If we find a new finale model,

943
00:56:17,800 --> 00:56:19,570
we'll alter the dress and put her in it immediately,

944
00:56:19,840 --> 00:56:21,240
so stay on your toes.

945
00:56:21,610 --> 00:56:23,780
But what if we can't find a model for the finale...

946
00:56:23,840 --> 00:56:24,880
That won't happen.

947
00:56:25,480 --> 00:56:27,680
I will make this Trunk Show a success.

948
00:56:28,450 --> 00:56:29,680
Okay.

949
00:56:33,220 --> 00:56:34,220
Sir.

950
00:56:34,350 --> 00:56:36,260
It seems they haven't found a finale model yet.

951
00:56:39,790 --> 00:56:42,900
The show is about to start, and if they still haven't found one,

952
00:56:43,600 --> 00:56:45,270
it's safe to say the finale is in jeopardy, right?

953
00:56:45,600 --> 00:56:46,600
What should we do?

954
00:56:46,900 --> 00:56:49,470
- We could hire one of our models... - Let's...

955
00:56:49,640 --> 00:56:50,640
just watch.

956
00:56:52,240 --> 00:56:55,010
Let's not cross the line. We'll wait for now.

957
00:56:55,610 --> 00:56:56,740
Yes, sir.

958
00:57:02,680 --> 00:57:04,480
She's on an overseas shoot?

959
00:57:05,490 --> 00:57:06,920
Yes, I see. Nothing we can do, then.

960
00:57:07,720 --> 00:57:08,720
Yes.

961
00:57:09,260 --> 00:57:11,290
What are we going to do?

962
00:57:11,720 --> 00:57:13,360
Has no one said yes yet?

963
00:57:13,730 --> 00:57:14,730
No.

964
00:57:14,790 --> 00:57:17,360
Of all times, it's during Fashion Week.

965
00:57:18,260 --> 00:57:20,500
Doesn't anyone know someone they can call?

966
00:57:24,240 --> 00:57:27,310
What do we do? The show's about to start.

967
00:57:27,740 --> 00:57:29,340
What's the plan, CEO Baek?

968
00:57:33,680 --> 00:57:37,180
We will now begin the Trunk Show for Bruni & Co. and J&White.

969
00:58:06,850 --> 00:58:08,050
Who did they say is doing the finale?

970
00:58:08,280 --> 00:58:10,850
I heard they haven't found anyone yet.

971
00:58:10,950 --> 00:58:12,690
This is a complete disaster.

972
00:58:22,460 --> 00:58:25,160
The finale is in ten minutes.

973
00:58:27,870 --> 00:58:29,240
We're so screwed.

974
00:58:29,700 --> 00:58:31,800
Where did the two CEOs go?

975
00:58:34,540 --> 00:58:35,780
Good question.

976
00:58:37,110 --> 00:58:39,880
Are they off crying in a corner somewhere?

977
00:58:40,410 --> 00:58:41,410
No.

978
00:58:42,550 --> 00:58:44,220
The finale is in ten minutes.

979
00:58:44,280 --> 00:58:45,750
I know. So why are we here?

980
00:58:46,050 --> 00:58:48,220
Ji Won Ho, you can do an alteration right now, can't you?

981
00:58:48,520 --> 00:58:49,820
An alteration? Here?

982
00:58:50,020 --> 00:58:51,020
What are you talking about?

983
00:58:51,760 --> 00:58:53,630
The finale is going on as planned.

984
00:58:53,790 --> 00:58:55,230
How? We don't have a model.

985
00:58:56,300 --> 00:58:57,300
I'm doing it.

986
00:58:57,560 --> 00:58:58,560
What?

987
00:59:03,470 --> 00:59:05,710
Ji Won Ho, I'm giving you ten minutes.

988
00:59:30,900 --> 00:59:32,130
And now for tonight's highlight.

989
00:59:32,470 --> 00:59:34,400
Our finale model makes her entrance.

990
01:00:26,090 --> 01:00:28,050
(Special Thanks to Lee Su Ji for Her Guest Appearance)

991
01:00:40,630 --> 01:00:43,570
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

992
01:00:45,200 --> 01:00:48,140
I don't see why not. Let's do it. The collaboration.

993
01:00:48,470 --> 01:00:51,680
- What? - Don't ruin this. Get on board.

994
01:00:51,740 --> 01:00:53,610
What do you mean, "get on board?"

995
01:00:53,680 --> 01:00:58,280
- What, am I your puppy? - Like the calm before the storm.

996
01:00:58,350 --> 01:00:59,990
Why Calvin got divorced...

997
01:01:00,350 --> 01:01:02,220
I came because I have something to give you in person.

998
01:01:02,390 --> 01:01:05,660
The vibe between them was definitely different than usual.

999
01:01:06,290 --> 01:01:07,290
And if I don't stay put?

1000
01:01:07,360 --> 01:01:08,460
Then I'll have to do something more.

1001
01:01:09,960 --> 01:01:11,500
Revenge?
